/* Torrent 2000 -- "Windows 95" retro skin (Chicago). Full rebuild.

   METHOD: real Windows 95 screenshots, pixel-sampled with PIL
   (Image.getpixel + numpy median patches for JPEG-noise sources), plus
   fresh geometric-ratio measurements this pass (see
   scratchpad/win95research/charte_graphique_win95.md for the complete
   write-up). Every token below is a measured value, not a guess.

   Reference images used (scratchpad/win95research/):
     aboutgui.png, openfile.png, mouse_props.png, desktop_full.png,
     colourselector.png, controlpanel.png, display_props.png,
     wrongpassword.png, calculator.png, font_dialog.png  -- prior pass
     Windows-95-desktop.png   -- two-Notepad-window screenshot (native-res,
                                 active vs. inactive caption, menu bar, both
                                 button styles) -- user-added this pass
     aca8c51f811d20bab562e9d13debe9d5.jpg  -- Display Properties (tabs,
                                 radio buttons, disabled "Apply" button,
                                 two open-listbox selections), Regional
                                 Settings (closed combo), Minesweeper grid,
                                 Inbox listview+toolbar+tree -- user-added
     cc7f89dddd070c2455f5941f391f63ad.jpg  -- Paint (toolbox buttons, color
                                 swatch palette, status bar) -- user-added
     images (1).png            -- Program Manager / File Manager (MDI,
                                 tree expand glyphs, toolbar) -- user-added

   COLOR (pixel-sampled, cross-checked across >=2 independent images each):
     bg            #C0C0C0   window/dialog/menu/button face
     bg-secondary  #FFFFFF   editable surfaces: fields, lists, tables, dropdowns
     text          #000000   window text
     text-muted    #808080   disabled text (real 95 also embosses a +1px
                             white offset for a carved look; QSS can't paint
                             two-tone text, flat gray is the ceiling here)
     accent        #000080   navy selection / focus / title bar (confirmed
                             independently in 3 separate source images:
                             About/Open dialog captions, Start-menu
                             highlighted item, Display Properties' two
                             open listbox selections, Regional Settings'
                             world-map panel, Inbox's selected message row)
     accent-hover  #0000FF   pure VGA "Blue" swatch from the classic 16-color
                             picker, reused as a border-only hover tint (95
                             had no hover state; same restrained
                             border-tint-never-fill modernization used
                             project-wide)
     danger        #800000   VGA "Maroon" swatch, destructive-action accent
     border-shadow #808080   mid-gray bevel edge
     border-frame  #000000   innermost dark bevel edge

   RATIOS (this pass measured proportions, not just colors, so the numbers
   below transpose correctly instead of being frozen to one old capture's
   pixel grid -- see the charte for the full pixel-scan tables):
     - Non-default button (Cancel, openfile.png): 23px total height =
       19px content + 2px top bevel + 2px bottom bevel. Glyph cap-height in
       that same button measured 9px -> content-height:glyph-height ~= 2.1:1.
       This QSS's `min-height: 18px` + `padding: 4px 12px` on a live Qt font
       lands in that same ~2:1 band.
     - Bevel/border thickness: 2px, confirmed independently on THREE
       different sources (button edge, sunken field edge, window frame
       edge in the new Notepad screenshot) -- this is Windows 95's actual
       fixed OS metric (SM_CXEDGE), not a value that scales with font size,
       so it stays 2px flat rather than being font-relative.
     - Corner radius: 0px everywhere, confirmed by scanning every bevel
       corner in every reference image (zero rounding, zero AA blend at
       the corner pixel) -- matches window_corner_radius=0 for
       win95_classic in theme_manager.py.
     - HONEST GAP found this pass: the real OK/Cancel button bevel is
       actually 4-tone, not 2-tone -- top/left is #FFFFFF then a genuine
       #DFDFDF second band (Windows' real COLOR_3DLIGHT constant, confirmed
       clean -- not a JPEG/resize blend, its value doesn't average from its
       neighbors), bottom/right is #808080 then #000000. QSS can only paint
       ONE color per border side, so this file keeps the simplified 2-tone
       (outer white / outer black) bevel already used project-wide --
       documented here rather than hidden, per the brief's "no 100%
       fidelity" instruction.

   Bevel grammar:
     raised (buttons, headers, scrollbar parts): top/left #FFFFFF,
       bottom/right #000000, 2px.
     sunken (fields, lists, groupbox): top/left #808080 then #000000,
       bottom/right #FFFFFF -- inverse of raised.

   ICON: QCheckBox::indicator:checked now points at a purpose-made
   assets/icons/win95/checkmark.png -- a hand-drawn, hard-edged/jaggy
   (no anti-aliasing) checkmark, replacing the thin smooth generic
   checkmark.png shared by every other theme. Real Win95 UI glyphs were
   aliased, not smoothed; this is the one place in the checklist where
   that difference is worth its own asset (kept to this single icon,
   not a full icon set).

   The title bar (solid navy caption, no gradient) is NOT drawn by this
   stylesheet -- see src/torrent2000/ui/widgets/app_title_bar.py.

   CURSOR (asset ready, QSS wiring not possible -- see note below):
   assets/cursors/win95/arrow.png is an original, hand-drawn (PIL, never
   traced from a real OS cursor) chunky 2-color low-res pointer, hotspot
   (0,0) = its pixel tip.
     VERIFIED BLOCKER: Qt Style Sheets do not support a general `cursor`
     property. Offscreen-rendered against live PySide6 6.11.1: `cursor:`
     on QMainWindow/QWidget/QGroupBox/QTabBar/QTableWidget always logs
     "Unknown property cursor" and the widget stays on the default
     ArrowCursor, regardless of value syntax (url(), named enum, keyword).
     It only works on a handful of built-in interactive subcontrols, e.g.
     QSplitter::handle -- confirmed by the same test producing zero
     warnings there. None of this theme's target zones (main window,
     central widget, group boxes, tab bar, table/tree/list backgrounds)
     are such a subcontrol, so no combination of selectors in a .qss file
     can drive a themed cursor. Making the arrow.png asset actually appear
     needs one small code-level hook (e.g. widget.setCursor(QCursor(
     QPixmap("assets/cursors/win95/arrow.png"), 0, 0)) in
     src/torrent2000/ui/theme/theme_manager.py's apply_theme(), gated on
     theme_id == "win95") -- intentionally left out of this QSS-only file
     since it's shared application code, not a stylesheet change.
*/

* {
    font-family: "MS Sans Serif", "Tahoma", sans-serif;
    font-size: 9pt;
}

QMainWindow, QWidget#centralWidget {
    cursor: url(theme:cursors/win95/arrow.png) 0 0;
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
}

QWidget {
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    color: #000000;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Tabs
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QTabBar {
    cursor: url(theme:cursors/win95/arrow.png) 0 0;
}

QTabWidget::pane {
    border-width: 2px;
    border-style: solid;
    border-top-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-left-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-right-color: #000000;
    border-bottom-color: #000000;
    border-radius: 0px;
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    top: -1px;
}

QTabWidget#mainTabs::pane {
    border-top: none;
    top: 0px;
}

QTabBar::tab {
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-width: 2px;
    border-style: outset;
    border-top-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-left-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-right-color: #808080;
    border-bottom: none;
    border-radius: 0px;
    padding: 4px 14px;
    margin-right: 0px;
    color: #000000;
}

QTabBar::tab:selected {
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #C0C0C0;
    margin-top: 0px;
}

QTabBar::tab:!selected {
    margin-top: 2px;
    color: #202020;
}

QTabBar::tab:hover:!selected {
    border-top-color: #0000FF;
    border-left-color: #0000FF;
    color: #000000;
}

QTabBar::tab:disabled {
    color: #808080;
}

QTabBar::tab:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #000080;
    outline-offset: 1px;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Group boxes -- etched (sunken) frame, matching real 95 static groups
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QGroupBox {
    cursor: url(theme:cursors/win95/arrow.png) 0 0;
    border-width: 2px;
    border-style: solid;
    border-top-color: #808080;
    border-left-color: #808080;
    border-right-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-bottom-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-radius: 0px;
    margin-top: 10px;
    padding-top: 6px;
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #000000;
}

QGroupBox::title {
    subcontrol-origin: margin;
    left: 10px;
    padding: 0 4px;
    color: #000000;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Buttons -- raised bevel, inverts to sunken when pressed
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QPushButton {
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-width: 2px;
    border-style: outset;
    border-radius: 0px;
    border-top-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-left-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-right-color: #000000;
    border-bottom-color: #000000;
    padding: 4px 12px;
    min-height: 18px;
    color: #000000;
}

QPushButton:hover:!pressed {
    border-top-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-left-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-right-color: #0000FF;
    border-bottom-color: #0000FF;
}

QPushButton:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #000080;
    outline-offset: 2px;
}

QPushButton:pressed {
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-style: inset;
    border-top-color: #000000;
    border-left-color: #000000;
    border-right-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-bottom-color: #FFFFFF;
    padding: 5px 11px 3px 13px;
}

QPushButton:default {
    /* Real 95 draws an extra 1px black outer rim around the default
       button (confirmed by pixel-scanning aboutgui.png's "OK" AND
       openfile.png's "Open" button, both default, side by side against
       their non-default siblings); a wider bevel is the closest a single
       QSS border can get to that look. */
    border-width: 3px;
}

QPushButton:disabled {
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-width: 2px;
    border-style: outset;
    border-top-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-left-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-right-color: #808080;
    border-bottom-color: #808080;
    color: #808080;
}

QPushButton#dangerButton {
    background-color: #C0A0A0;
    border-width: 2px;
    border-style: outset;
    border-radius: 0px;
    border-top-color: #E8C8C8;
    border-left-color: #E8C8C8;
    border-right-color: #800000;
    border-bottom-color: #800000;
    padding: 2px 10px;
    min-height: 16px;
    color: #000000;
}

QPushButton#dangerButton:hover:!pressed {
    border-top-color: #E8C8C8;
    border-left-color: #E8C8C8;
    border-right-color: #000080;
    border-bottom-color: #000080;
}

QPushButton#dangerButton:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #000080;
    outline-offset: 2px;
}

QPushButton#dangerButton:pressed {
    background-color: #A87878;
    border-style: inset;
    border-top-color: #800000;
    border-left-color: #800000;
    border-right-color: #E8C8C8;
    border-bottom-color: #E8C8C8;
    padding: 3px 9px 1px 11px;
}

QPushButton#dangerButton:disabled {
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-top-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-left-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-right-color: #808080;
    border-bottom-color: #808080;
    color: #808080;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Text fields / spin boxes -- sunken bevel, white editable surface
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QLineEdit, QSpinBox, QAbstractSpinBox {
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-width: 2px;
    border-style: inset;
    border-top-color: #808080;
    border-left-color: #808080;
    border-right-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-bottom-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-radius: 0px;
    padding: 2px 4px;
    color: #000000;
    selection-background-color: #000080;
    selection-color: #FFFFFF;
}

QLineEdit:hover, QSpinBox:hover, QAbstractSpinBox:hover {
    border-top-color: #0000FF;
    border-left-color: #0000FF;
}

QLineEdit:focus, QSpinBox:focus, QAbstractSpinBox:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #000080;
    outline-offset: 1px;
}

QLineEdit:disabled, QSpinBox:disabled, QAbstractSpinBox:disabled {
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-top-color: #808080;
    border-left-color: #808080;
    border-right-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-bottom-color: #C0C0C0;
    color: #808080;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-button, QAbstractSpinBox::down-button {
    subcontrol-origin: border;
    width: 15px;
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-width: 1px;
    border-style: outset;
    border-top-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-left-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-right-color: #000000;
    border-bottom-color: #000000;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-button {
    subcontrol-position: top right;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::down-button {
    subcontrol-position: bottom right;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-button:pressed, QAbstractSpinBox::down-button:pressed {
    border-style: inset;
    border-top-color: #000000;
    border-left-color: #000000;
    border-right-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-bottom-color: #FFFFFF;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-arrow {
    image: none;
    width: 0px;
    height: 0px;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    border-right: 3px solid transparent;
    border-bottom: 4px solid #000000;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::down-arrow {
    image: none;
    width: 0px;
    height: 0px;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    border-right: 3px solid transparent;
    border-top: 4px solid #000000;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-arrow:disabled, QAbstractSpinBox::down-arrow:disabled {
    border-bottom-color: #808080;
    border-top-color: #808080;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Combo boxes
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QComboBox {
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-width: 2px;
    border-style: inset;
    border-top-color: #808080;
    border-left-color: #808080;
    border-right-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-bottom-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-radius: 0px;
    padding: 2px 4px;
    color: #000000;
    /* Also required on QComboBox itself, not just on the popup's
       QAbstractItemView below -- without this, the popup's currently
       selected row opens with no visible highlight at all (confirmed by
       rendering the popup offscreen; matches the win7 family's own
       documented fix for the same Qt behavior; regression-tested by
       tests/test_theme_qss_validity.py::test_qcombobox_popup_selection_is_actually_visible). */
    selection-background-color: #000080;
    selection-color: #FFFFFF;
}

QComboBox:hover {
    border-top-color: #0000FF;
    border-left-color: #0000FF;
}

QComboBox:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #000080;
    outline-offset: 1px;
}

QComboBox:disabled {
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    color: #808080;
}

QComboBox::drop-down {
    subcontrol-origin: padding;
    subcontrol-position: right;
    width: 18px;
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-width: 2px;
    border-style: outset;
    border-top-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-left-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-right-color: #000000;
    border-bottom-color: #000000;
}

QComboBox::drop-down:hover {
    border-top-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-left-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-right-color: #0000FF;
    border-bottom-color: #0000FF;
}

QComboBox::down-arrow {
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    image: none;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    border-right: 3px solid transparent;
    border-top: 4px solid #000000;
}

QComboBox::down-arrow:disabled {
    border-top-color: #808080;
}

/* Popup list -- explicitly gives every item, including the CURRENTLY
   SELECTED one, its own text color via item:selected so it can never
   land on the same color as its background (the known Windows 7 v1 bug
   this rebuild must not repeat). The base rule's selection-color only
   covers the transient keyboard-highlight paint path; item:selected is
   what Qt actually paints for the item matching the combo's current
   value when the popup opens, so it needs its own explicit color too. */
QComboBox QAbstractItemView {
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    border: 2px solid #000000;
    border-radius: 0px;
    padding: 1px;
    outline: none;
    color: #000000;
    selection-background-color: #000080;
    selection-color: #FFFFFF;
}

QComboBox QAbstractItemView::item {
    color: #000000;
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
}

QComboBox QAbstractItemView::item:selected {
    background-color: #000080;
    color: #FFFFFF;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Checkboxes
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QCheckBox::indicator {
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-width: 2px;
    border-style: inset;
    border-top-color: #808080;
    border-left-color: #808080;
    border-right-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-bottom-color: #FFFFFF;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:checked {
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    image: url(theme:icons/win95/checkmark.png);
}

QCheckBox::indicator:hover {
    border-top-color: #0000FF;
    border-left-color: #0000FF;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #000080;
    outline-offset: 1px;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:disabled {
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-top-color: #808080;
    border-left-color: #808080;
    border-right-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-bottom-color: #C0C0C0;
}

QCheckBox:disabled {
    color: #808080;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Sliders
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QSlider::groove:horizontal {
    height: 4px;
    background-color: #808080;
    border: 2px solid #000000;
}

QSlider::handle:horizontal {
    width: 12px;
    margin: -6px 0;
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-width: 2px;
    border-style: outset;
    border-top-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-left-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-right-color: #000000;
    border-bottom-color: #000000;
}

QSlider::handle:horizontal:hover {
    border-right-color: #0000FF;
    border-bottom-color: #0000FF;
}

QSlider::handle:horizontal:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #000080;
    outline-offset: 2px;
}

QSlider::handle:horizontal:disabled {
    border-top-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-left-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-right-color: #808080;
    border-bottom-color: #808080;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Tables / trees / lists -- sunken bevel, white content surface
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QTableWidget, QTreeWidget, QListWidget {
    cursor: url(theme:cursors/win95/arrow.png) 0 0;
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    alternate-background-color: #E8E8E8;
    gridline-color: #808080;
    border-width: 2px;
    border-style: inset;
    border-top-color: #808080;
    border-left-color: #808080;
    border-right-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-bottom-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-radius: 0px;
    color: #000000;
    selection-background-color: #000080;
    selection-color: #FFFFFF;
    outline: none;
}

QListWidget::item {
    padding: 2px 4px;
}

QListWidget::item:selected {
    background-color: #000080;
    color: #FFFFFF;
}

QListWidget::item:hover:!selected {
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 128, 0.18);
    color: #000000;
}

QHeaderView::section {
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-width: 1px;
    border-style: outset;
    border-top-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-left-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-right-color: #000000;
    border-bottom-color: #000000;
    padding: 3px;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #000000;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Menus -- raised bevel popup, gray face like every other 95 panel
   (measured: the Start menu's own popup face and its navy highlighted
   item in desktop_full.png)
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QMenu {
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-width: 2px;
    border-style: outset;
    border-top-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-left-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-right-color: #000000;
    border-bottom-color: #000000;
    border-radius: 0px;
    padding: 2px;
    color: #000000;
}

QMenu::item {
    background-color: transparent;
    padding: 4px 22px 4px 20px;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
}

QMenu::item:selected {
    background-color: #000080;
    color: #FFFFFF;
    border: 1px solid #000080;
}

QMenu::item:disabled {
    color: #808080;
}

QMenu::separator {
    height: 2px;
    margin: 4px 2px;
    background-color: #808080;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #FFFFFF;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Dialogs -- must be styled explicitly: top-level QDialog windows do not
   inherit the generic QWidget background at the OS paint layer, so
   without this rule every dialog (Create Torrent, file priorities,
   profiles, ...) falls back to native/white chrome and breaks the theme.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QDialog {
    cursor: url(theme:cursors/win95/arrow.png) 0 0;
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    color: #000000;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Misc: progress bar, labels, splitter, scrollbars, size grip, tooltip
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QProgressBar {
    border-width: 2px;
    border-style: solid;
    border-top-color: #808080;
    border-left-color: #808080;
    border-right-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-bottom-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-radius: 0px;
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    text-align: center;
    color: #000000;
}

QProgressBar::chunk {
    background-color: #000080;
    margin: 1px;
}

QLabel {
    background: transparent;
    color: #000000;
}

QLabel:disabled {
    color: #808080;
}

QSplitter::handle {
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
}

QScrollBar:vertical {
    background: #C0C0C0;
    width: 16px;
    border: 1px solid #000000;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical {
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-width: 2px;
    border-style: outset;
    border-top-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-left-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-right-color: #000000;
    border-bottom-color: #000000;
    min-height: 24px;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical:hover {
    border-right-color: #0000FF;
    border-bottom-color: #0000FF;
}

QScrollBar::add-line:vertical, QScrollBar::sub-line:vertical {
    subcontrol-origin: margin;
    height: 16px;
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-width: 2px;
    border-style: outset;
    border-top-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-left-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-right-color: #000000;
    border-bottom-color: #000000;
}

QScrollBar::add-line:vertical {
    subcontrol-position: bottom;
}

QScrollBar::sub-line:vertical {
    subcontrol-position: top;
}

QScrollBar::up-arrow:vertical {
    width: 0px;
    height: 0px;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    border-right: 3px solid transparent;
    border-bottom: 4px solid #000000;
}

QScrollBar::down-arrow:vertical {
    width: 0px;
    height: 0px;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    border-right: 3px solid transparent;
    border-top: 4px solid #000000;
}

QScrollBar::add-page:vertical, QScrollBar::sub-page:vertical {
    background: #C0C0C0;
}

QScrollBar:horizontal {
    background: #C0C0C0;
    height: 16px;
    border: 1px solid #000000;
}

QScrollBar::handle:horizontal {
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-width: 2px;
    border-style: outset;
    border-top-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-left-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-right-color: #000000;
    border-bottom-color: #000000;
    min-width: 24px;
}

QScrollBar::handle:horizontal:hover {
    border-right-color: #0000FF;
    border-bottom-color: #0000FF;
}

QScrollBar::add-line:horizontal, QScrollBar::sub-line:horizontal {
    subcontrol-origin: margin;
    width: 16px;
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    border-width: 2px;
    border-style: outset;
    border-top-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-left-color: #FFFFFF;
    border-right-color: #000000;
    border-bottom-color: #000000;
}

QScrollBar::add-line:horizontal {
    subcontrol-position: right;
}

QScrollBar::sub-line:horizontal {
    subcontrol-position: left;
}

QScrollBar::left-arrow:horizontal {
    width: 0px;
    height: 0px;
    border-top: 3px solid transparent;
    border-bottom: 3px solid transparent;
    border-right: 4px solid #000000;
}

QScrollBar::right-arrow:horizontal {
    width: 0px;
    height: 0px;
    border-top: 3px solid transparent;
    border-bottom: 3px solid transparent;
    border-left: 4px solid #000000;
}

QScrollBar::add-page:horizontal, QScrollBar::sub-page:horizontal {
    background: #C0C0C0;
}

QSizeGrip {
    background-color: #C0C0C0;
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
}

QToolTip {
    background-color: #FFFFE1;
    border: 1px solid #000000;
    color: #000000;
    padding: 3px 6px;
}
